  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Bowling balls come in 111111 total sizes, an integer weight between 666 and 161616 (measured in pounds).\n\nIn a bowling event, Chef is given a total of NNN bowling balls, with the iii-th one being AiA_iAi​ pounds. Some of the bowling balls may have the same weight as the others.\n\nChef can use a bowling ball which is at least XXX pounds, and at most YYY pounds. Find the number of bowling balls Chef can use.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 333 integers - N,XN, XN,X and YYY.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of bowling balls Chef can use.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "6≤X≤Y≤166 \\le X \\le Y \\le 166≤X≤Y≤16",
      "6≤Ai≤166 \\le A_i \\le 166≤Ai​≤16"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 7 10\n6 8 10 11\n5 6 16\n6 16 16 9 9\n1 7 10\n16",
        "output": "2\n5\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Chef can use the second and third bowling balls.\nTest Case 2 : Chef can use all the bowling balls.\nTest Case 3 : Chef can use none of the bowling balls."
      }
    ]
  },
